Hi-
  I have ascended many a Wizard, and I am surprised that nobody else
mirrors my opinions on the best first wishes for young Mages.

SPOILERS FOLLOW:






  Wizards are by far the SINGLE EASIEST CHARACTER to win with, once
you know their tricks.  Of course, this may involve certain well-known
spoilers, that some consider cheating, but are well within the scope of
the game.
  There is a reason why the ATHAME cannot be gained by either polypiling
or sacrificing.  Only Wizards, and the finders-of-dead-wizards can get
one.  I have been known to wish for an Athame when playing less well-
endowed characters, such as Barbarians and Tourists. :)
  This much said, when your first level wizard is granted a wish, do
not wish for +3 back dragon scale mail.  Do not wish for speed boots,
Mjollnir, Excalibur, Fire Brand, a Helm of Telepathy, Amulet of Life
Saving, cursed scrolls of genocide, blessed potions of gain ability, or
any other such minor trinkets.
  Wish first and foremost for a ring of LEVITATION.  If you have this
already, get a ring of conflict too.  You will now win the game.  Don't
forget that that nice cloak of magic resistance also comes in handy.  If
you still feel that a Wizard's best wish is for Fire Brand or whatever,
go play a Barbarian and leave the Wizarding to the Wizards.

  Once you have these items, go ahead and wish for the weapons and armor
that are so prized by the other mortals.

